questions.question:
If &nbsp;&nbsp; A = $$\left[ {\matrix{
   { - 4} &amp; { - 1}  \cr 
   3 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right]$$, 
<br><br>then the determinant of the matrix (A<sup>2016</sup> − 2A<sup>2015</sup> − A<sup>2014</sup>) is :

questions.explanation:
Given,


$$A = \left[ {\matrix{
   { - 4} &amp; { - 1}  \cr 
   3 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right]$$


${A^2} = \left[ {\matrix{
   { - 4} &amp; { - 1}  \cr 
   3 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right]\left[ {\matrix{
   { - 4} &amp; { - 1}  \cr 
   3 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right]$$


$$ = \left[ {\matrix{
   {13} &amp; 3  \cr 
   { - 9} &amp; { - 2}  \cr 

 } } \right]$$


A<sup>2</sup> $$-$$ 2A $$-$$ I


$$ = \left[ {\matrix{
   {13} &amp; 3  \cr 
   { - 9} &amp; { - 2}  \cr 

 } } \right] - \left[ {\matrix{
   { - 8} &amp; { - 2}  \cr 
   6 &amp; 2  \cr 

 } } \right] - \left[ {\matrix{
   1 &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right]$$


$$ = \left[ {\matrix{
   {20} &amp; 5  \cr 
   { - 15} &amp; { - 5}  \cr 

 } } \right]$$


$$\left| A \right| = \left| {\matrix{
   { - 4} &amp; { - 1}  \cr 
   3 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right|$$ $$=$$ $$-$$ 4 + 3 $$=$$ $$-$$ 1


Now, 


$$\left| {{A^{2016}} - 2{A^{2015}} - {A^{2014}}} \right|$$


$$=$$ ${\left| A \right|^{2014}}\left| {{A^2} - 2A - {\rm I}} \right|$$


$$ = {\left( { - 1} \right)^{2014}}\left| {\matrix{
   {20} &amp; 5  \cr 
   { - 15} &amp; { - 5}  \cr 

 } } \right|$$


$$=$$ 1 $$ \times $$ ($$-$$ 100 + 75)


$$=$$ $$-$$ 25
